# Same idea as .gitignore, but for `docker build`: this defines what never gets sent to the
# Docker daemon as the build context in the first place (everything under the path you pass to
# `docker build`, e.g. the repo root here — before it even reads the Dockerfile). Anything listed
# here is invisible to every COPY instruction, no matter what it asks for. That's what keeps the
# build context small and stops locally-built (host-platform) binaries from accidentally getting
# copied into the image instead of being rebuilt inside it.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/

.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.editorconfig
*.slnx

docs/
tools/
README.md
CLAUDE.md
LICENSE.md
